2026-11-06T02:56:57.2396011Z [34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
2026-11-06T02:56:57.2406465Z [0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
2026-11-06T02:56:57.2407318Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
2026-11-06T02:56:57.2412723Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
2026-11-06T02:56:57.2413028Z 
2026-11-06T02:56:57.2413453Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
2026-11-06T02:56:57.2413739Z 
2026-11-06T02:56:57.2413970Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
2026-11-06T02:56:57.2414423Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
2026-11-06T02:56:57.2414825Z 
2026-11-06T02:56:57.2414956Z If you would like to
2026-11-06T02:56:57.2415317Z see the output, try like this:
2026-11-06T02:56:57.2415566Z 
2026-11-06T02:56:57.2415859Z   $ curl -L -o install-nix https://nixos.org/nix/install
2026-11-06T02:56:57.2416303Z   $ sh ./install-nix
